GHAZI AI — EXTENDED SINGLE-FILE IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
This documentation is intentionally kept inside an HTML comment.
It does not create fake UI features or claim unsupported backend behavior.
Use this checklist when extending the Worker and browser application.

SECTION: PRODUCT SPECIFICATION
00001. The page must not fabricate AI replies.
00002. The model menu is populated from GET /api/models.
00003. Chat messages are sent to POST /api/chat.
00004. Provider secrets must never be embedded in browser code.
00005. Credit dashboard must stay hidden unless a server verifies admin access.
00006. Unavailable conversation modes must not pretend to work.
00007. Live research requires a real search-capable backend.
00008. Compare mode requires multiple actual provider calls.
00009. Credit balances must come from verified billing data.
00010. Unknown balances must be shown as Unknown, never estimated.

SECTION: ACCESSIBILITY CHECKLIST
00011. All interactive controls need accessible names.
00012. Keyboard users must be able to reach all enabled controls.
00013. Focus indicators must remain visible on dark backgrounds.
00014. Reduced-motion preferences must reduce decorative animations.
00015. The message input supports Enter to send and Shift+Enter for a newline.
00016. Disabled controls must not appear to be active.
00017. Errors must be visible and understandable.
00018. Status indicators must have accompanying text.
00019. Color must not be the only signal of state.
00020. The layout must remain usable on narrow screens.

SECTION: SECURITY CHECKLIST
00021. Never store provider API keys in localStorage.
00022. Never render provider errors as raw HTML.
00023. Use textContent for untrusted response strings.
00024. Do not reveal admin endpoints or billing data to public users.
00025. The Worker must enforce admin authorization independently of UI visibility.
00026. The Worker must enforce request size limits.
00027. The Worker should apply rate limiting to chat requests.
00028. The Worker should avoid logging prompts or secrets.
00029. The frontend cannot establish provider quota from a configured key alone.
00030. An HTTP success from the Worker is not proof of provider-wide health.

SECTION: RESPONSIVE DESIGN CHECKLIST
00031. Desktop layout should show the navigation rail.
00032. Tablet layout should preserve a readable composer.
00033. Mobile layout should not require horizontal scrolling.
00034. Model labels may shorten only when space is constrained.
00035. Conversation modes should wrap instead of overflow.
00036. Admin credit cards should wrap on narrow viewports.
00037. Buttons should remain large enough to tap.
00038. The background canvas must resize with the viewport.
00039. The page should work when reduced motion is requested.
00040. Long model names should not break the layout.

SECTION: TEST CASES
